  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_069a1bc35b8941a6b996f626ce9187a0",
      "statement": "step ca renew takes exactly two positional arguments, defaults --out to overwriting the input certificate and --root to pki.GetRootCAPath(), makes --expires-in and --renew-period mutually exclusive, requires --renew-period with --daemon, and requires both to be shorter than the certificate validity period.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L233-L321",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:00969ead325b6bea32e89cd4f00bd70a139ec7c799b790785d7dc29cf38ff32a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c72a140010c14f3f888df20c9171bfe6",
      "statement": "renew loads the key KMS-aware via tlsLoadX509KeyPair using cryptoutil.CreateSigner (so --kms URIs and --password-file decryption work), and supports --pid/--pid-file (mutually exclusive) with --signal defaulting to SIGHUP.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L280-L306",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:099ab502e7ad66998da4b743d440fef7cc4d850a2ba0f254ebd56d6f78aa1a56:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L656-L679",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dc4f47665c749786f32ce06dccd6dfd6a4243c75bf4dce9efeb757fc1eac02f4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2e679622ef9e439cbf1157ec04b0dbda",
      "statement": "newRenewer builds an http.Transport rooted at --root and attaches the client certificate for mTLS only if the certificate is still valid; --offline swaps in the in-process authority client requiring --ca-config.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L425-L480",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:33a946aa7797b12818ee4247cbe7f3f5ea0f6174ea66a69cec015ff70832392f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_40feba9540c64896bb2c80fed9022079",
      "statement": "renewer.Renew uses the token flow when --mtls=false or the certificate is already expired (enabling renew-after-expiry where the CA allows it), otherwise mTLS client.Renew(transport); the help text documents L7 proxies, missing clientAuth EKU, and StepCAS RA as reasons to force --mtls=false.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L482-L508",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ca6955608fbd22d95d3462b222f6f3303c82d695982f4f43bc06ef112d795486:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L68-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ba5ab0464096fb6ccc996e3255193062a5a1273c3741ebd795c5b1dc8800b97c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7b3a02d007744fbc855f4362bf3a53c6",
      "statement": "RenewWithToken builds a provisioner-independent renewal JWT with audience <caURL>/renew, issuer step-ca-client/1.0, subject equal to the leaf common name, and an x5cInsecure header carrying the full chain signed by the certificate's own key; it clears the client cert from the transport and closes idle connections so daemons never reuse a certificate-less connection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L624-L654",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:074dd79cf702b2040bf5d4778074a61dfd668c75d627dde633389f71e88d91cb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a04c5f068d5741d0b94d135cba528ec9",
      "statement": "The renewal response chain (CertChainPEM or ServerPEM+CaPEM fallback) is serialized and written with fileutil.WriteFile mode 0o600.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L492-L505",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c31d79d80262631b15fe10a264f10ad49ccea7f29cd93830382d3d3c25334831:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_881f8b39ceb34a449f39b49bb4eaaa95",
      "statement": "One-shot renewal is skipped when notAfter - now > expiresIn + rand(expiresIn/20), printing 'certificate not renewed'; overwrite uses the standard prompt unless --force; after renewal the --pid/--pid-file target is signaled (default SIGHUP) and --exec runs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L336-L351",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2fbdbdcf524979596aeb09909ef4a4527eb9f66237f6f5b7b7acd349981a6ff9:"
