        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8c5480cb450445d79689e2a15f2f3d57",
      "statement": "Each daemon cycle renews, rewrites the file, rebuilds the tls.Certificate from the new chain keeping the same key (renewal never changes the key), updates the transport, and computes the next delay: fixed with --renew-period, otherwise renew after 2/3 of the validity period (expiresIn = period/3) minus jitter up to period/20, as documented in the help text.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L354-L380",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01ffbad2ae3f1aae3edb8f558cef5e6ddc34ca88f58078614ce4581c2896bcf8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L549-L584",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a0e71bdd184c47f8932c1867a0f00a3f9e4a5a41fdebebfd8fd25b58c90b0840:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L58-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19c602b343a40abb94e67f936af303ec3adbe3acf89ce863f2a7cbab8fda42ef:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cda66c5196af4f50b399d4587d916037",
      "statement": "step ca rekey rotates the key: KMS-backed keys require --private-key and forbid --out-key and --daemon because new KMS keys cannot be generated in-place, and expired certificates are rejected with 'cannot rekey an expired certificate'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/rekey.go#L249-L261",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d96a3498c69cdd04f0c8b00d84360ffb9edd502812459156c02211ee3dbb3128:"
